 "policy_v1": {
  "text": "ASTERON SYSTEMS PVT. LTD. - AI GOVERNANCE POLICY\nDocument ID: AIG-001 | Version 1.0\nDemo run: 5592c2\n\nDocument Control\nApproved by: Meera Khanna, Chief Information Security Officer\nApproval Date: 21 September 2026\nStatus: Approved and Published\n\n1. Purpose and legal requirements\nThis policy governs every AI system Asteron builds, buys or uses, including the AI agents that approve vendor purchases. The legal and regulatory requirements that apply to our AI systems are documented and kept current by the Legal team. Applicable regulations: EU AI Act, GDPR, Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023.\n\n2. Trustworthy AI\nAsteron's AI systems must be valid and reliable, safe, secure and resilient, and transparent and explainable.\n\n3. Risk tolerance and tiering\nAsteron's AI risk tolerance is defined and approved by the Risk Committee. Risk tiering criteria: impact on customers, autonomy of the system, and financial exposure per decision.\n\n4. Review\nThis policy and the AI governance programme are reviewed every 365 days.\n\n5. Roles\nEach AI system has a named business owner responsible for its decisions.\n\n6. Human oversight\nA named person oversees every high-impact AI system, including the purchasing agent.\n\n7. Training\nAll staff who build, buy or operate AI systems complete AI risk training every 365 days.\n\n8. Incidents\nAI incidents and failures follow a defined incident process. Report them to ai-incidents@asteron.example.\n\n9. Third-party AI\nThird-party AI systems, models and data are risk-assessed before purchase and annually after, under a defined third-party AI risk policy. Intellectual-property terms of every AI vendor are reviewed by Legal.",
